IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc3-listing.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II.1 Terrorism, "List of Entities": sections 83.05, 83.06 and 83.07.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), written by part agent ccc3 from the text alone. The text is a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws
-- Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
--
-- WHO THIS IS ABOUT. The list of entities is made by the Governor in Council on the Minister's recommendation. It is encoded for what it means to an
-- entity that is on it, or may be put on it, or shares a name with one: what the Minister and the Governor in Council may do to it, what it may apply for and by when,
-- and what a judge must do on review. There is no seat for an official (the brief).
--
-- READING A RESULT (rule of 2026-10-29 and the ruling of 2026-11-12): as in `ccc3-interpretation.l4`. A function named for a power ("may") answers NOTHING, not
-- JUST FALSE, when an "if" gate fails (tag GATE-A); a closed gate ("only if", "may not ... except if") answers JUST FALSE; a "may" function gated by a stated period
-- or by "within" answers JUST FALSE as the 2026-11-05 rulings say, and is listed for a lawyer (tag GATE-B). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Periods are dates (`Date day month year`); a day count is added with PLUS, a year count with `add years` (daydate).

§ `Section 83.05 -- Establishment of the list; applications to be removed`

§§ `83.05(1) to (1.2) establishing the list, the recommendation, changing a name`

-- (1) GATE-A: "may place any entity if, on the recommendation of the Minister ..., the Governor in Council is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe (a) or (b)".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-20 | s 83.05(1) the Governor in Council may place the entity on the list | s 83.05(1)*
-- src:1448 | Establishment of list
-- src:1449 | 83.05 (1) The Governor in Council may, by regulation, establish a list on which the Governor in Council may place any entity if, on the recommendation of the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness, the Governor in Council is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that
-- src:1450 | (a) the entity has knowingly carried out, attempted to carry out, participated in or facilitated a terrorist activity; or
-- src:1451 | (b) the entity has knowingly acted on behalf of, at the direction of or in association with an entity referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref s 83.05(1) (src:1448-1451)
GIVEN `the Governor in Council acts on the recommendation of the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the entity has knowingly carried out, attempted to carry out, participated in or facilitated a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the entity has knowingly acted on behalf of, at the direction of or in association with such an entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.05(1) the Governor in Council may place the entity on the list` MEANS
    IF     `the Governor in Council acts on the recommendation of the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness`
       AND (    `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the entity has knowingly carried out, attempted to carry out, participated in or facilitated a terrorist activity`
             OR `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the entity has knowingly acted on behalf of, at the direction of or in association with such an entity`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may place any entity if, on the recommendation of the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness, the Governor in Council is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that"

-- (1.1) a closed gate: "only if".
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.05(1.1) the Minister may make the recommendation | s 83.05(1.1)
-- src:1452 | Recommendation
-- src:1453 | (1.1) The Minister may make a recommendation referred to in subsection (1) only if he or she has reasonable grounds to believe that the entity to which the recommendation relates is an entity referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b).
@ref s 83.05(1.1) (src:1452-1453)
GIVEN `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that the entity to which the recommendation relates is an entity referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.05(1.1) the Minister may make the recommendation` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that the entity to which the recommendation relates is an entity referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may make a recommendation referred to in subsection (1) only if he or she has reasonable grounds to believe"

-- (1.2)(a) and (b) GATE-A: "may, by regulation, change the name ... if the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe ..."; "delete ... if the entity is no longer using that name".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-20 | s 83.05(1.2)(a) the Minister may change or add a name; s 83.05(1.2)(b) the Minister may delete a name | s 83.05(1.2)*
-- src:1454 | Amendment to name of listed entity
-- src:1455 | (1.2) The Minister may, by regulation,
-- src:1456 | (a) change the name of a listed entity, or add to the list any other name by which a listed entity may also be or have been known, if the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that the listed entity is using a name that is not on the list; and
-- src:1457 | (b) delete from the list any other name by which a listed entity may also have been known, if the entity is no longer using that name.
@ref s 83.05(1.2) (src:1454-1457)
GIVEN `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that the listed entity is using a name that is not on the list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.05(1.2)(a) the Minister may change or add a name` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that the listed entity is using a name that is not on the list`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that the listed entity is using a name that is not on the list"

@ref s 83.05(1.2) (src:1454-1457)
GIVEN `the entity is no longer using that name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.05(1.2)(b) the Minister may delete a name` MEANS
    IF `the entity is no longer using that name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the entity is no longer using that name"

§§ `83.05(2) to (4) the application to be removed: decision, deeming, notice`

-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6 | s 83.05(2) the Minister must decide the application | s 83.05(2)
-- src:1458 | Application to Minister
-- src:1459 | (2) On application in writing by a listed entity to be removed from the list, the Minister shall decide whether the applicant should remain a listed entity or whether the Minister should recommend to the Governor in Council that the applicant be removed from the list, taking into account the grounds set out in subsection (1).
@ref s 83.05(2) (src:1458-1459)
GIVEN `a listed entity has applied in writing to be removed from the list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.05(2) the Minister must decide the application` MEANS
    IF `a listed entity has applied in writing to be removed from the list`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application in writing by a listed entity to be removed from the list"

-- (3) "within 90 days after receipt of the application, or within any longer period that may be agreed to in writing". The deadline is receipt + 90 days, or the last day of the agreed longer period.
-- A decision on or before the deadline is in time; a decision after it, or none by it, is a failure to decide within the period.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.05(3) the Minister is deemed to have decided that the applicant should remain a listed entity | s 83.05(3)
-- src:1460 | Deeming
-- src:1461 | (3) If the Minister does not make a decision on the application referred to in subsection (2) within 90 days after receipt of the application, or within any longer period that may be agreed to in writing by the Minister and the applicant, the Minister is deemed to have decided that the applicant should remain a listed entity.
@ref s 83.05(3) (src:1460-1461)
GIVEN `the day of receipt of the application` IS A DATE
      `the last day of any longer period agreed to in writing` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the Minister decided, if the Minister has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.05(3) the Minister is deemed to have decided that the applicant should remain a listed entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the Minister decided, if the Minister has`
    WHEN JUST decided THEN
        IF decided AT MOST `the deadline`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Minister does not make a decision on the application referred to in subsection (2) within 90 days after receipt of the application"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the deadline`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the period is still running, so the text does not yet deem anything
    WHERE
        `the deadline` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the last day of any longer period agreed to in writing`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day of receipt of the application` PLUS 90
            WHEN JUST agreed THEN
                IF agreed GREATER THAN (`the day of receipt of the application` PLUS 90) THEN agreed ELSE (`the day of receipt of the application` PLUS 90)

-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6 | s 83.05(4) the Minister must give notice to the applicant without delay | s 83.05(4)
-- src:1462 | Notice of the decision to the applicant
-- src:1463 | (4) The Minister shall give notice without delay to the applicant of any decision taken or deemed to have been taken respecting the application referred to in subsection (2).
@ref s 83.05(4) (src:1462-1463)
GIVEN `a decision was taken or deemed to have been taken respecting the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.05(4) the Minister must give notice to the applicant without delay` MEANS
    IF `a decision was taken or deemed to have been taken respecting the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "of any decision taken or deemed to have been taken respecting the application referred to in subsection (2)"

§§ `83.05(5) to (7) judicial review of the decision`

-- (5) GATE-B: "Within 60 days after the receipt of the notice ... the applicant may apply to a judge for judicial review": a period gate on a "may" function.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-11 | s 83.05(5) the applicant may apply to a judge for judicial review | s 83.05(5)
-- src:1464 | Judicial review
-- src:1465 | (5) Within 60 days after the receipt of the notice of the decision referred to in subsection (4), the applicant may apply to a judge for judicial review of the decision.
@ref s 83.05(5) (src:1464-1465)
GIVEN `the day on which the notice of the decision was received` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the applicant applies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.05(5) the applicant may apply to a judge for judicial review` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the applicant applies` AT LEAST `the day on which the notice of the decision was received` AND `the day on which the applicant applies` AT MOST (`the day on which the notice of the decision was received` PLUS 60)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 60 days after the receipt of the notice of the decision referred to in subsection (4)"

-- (6)(c) and (d): the judge's duties; (a) and (b) are shown repealed. (d): "if found not to be reasonable, order that the applicant no longer be a listed entity".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6 | s 83.05(6)(c) the judge must provide the applicant with a reasonable opportunity to be heard; s 83.05(6)(d) the judge must order that the applicant no longer be a listed entity | s 83.05(6)*
-- src:1466 | Reference
-- src:1467 | (6) When an application is made under subsection (5), the judge shall, without delay
-- src:1468 | (a) [Repealed, 2024, c. 16, s. 89]
-- src:1469 | (b) [Repealed, 2024, c. 16, s. 89]
-- src:1470 | (c) provide the applicant with a reasonable opportunity to be heard; and
-- src:1471 | (d) determine whether the decision is reasonable on the basis of the information available to the judge and, if found not to be reasonable, order that the applicant no longer be a listed entity.
@ref s 83.05(6) (src:1466-1471)
GIVEN `the judge has provided the applicant with a reasonable opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.05(6)(c) the judge must provide the applicant with a reasonable opportunity to be heard` MEANS
    IF `the judge has provided the applicant with a reasonable opportunity to be heard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide the applicant with a reasonable opportunity to be heard"

@ref s 83.05(6) (src:1466-1471)
GIVEN `the judge finds the decision to be reasonable on the basis of the information available to the judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.05(6)(d) the judge must order that the applicant no longer be a listed entity` MEANS
    IF `the judge finds the decision to be reasonable on the basis of the information available to the judge`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if found not to be reasonable, order that the applicant no longer be a listed entity"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (6.1) "anything that, in the opinion of the judge, is reliable and appropriate, even if it would not otherwise be admissible under Canadian law".
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.05(6.1) the judge may receive the thing into evidence | s 83.05(6.1)
-- src:1472 | Evidence
-- src:1473 | (6.1) The judge may receive into evidence anything that, in the opinion of the judge, is reliable and appropriate, even if it would not otherwise be admissible under Canadian law, and may base his or her decision on that evidence.
@ref s 83.05(6.1) (src:1472-1473)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the judge the thing is reliable and appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.05(6.1) the judge may receive the thing into evidence` MEANS
    IF `in the opinion of the judge the thing is reliable and appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
