§ `Section 83.06 -- Return of information`

-- (1) "any information that is obtained in confidence from a government, ... and that is provided to the judge by the Minister ... shall be returned ... and shall not be considered ..., if (a), (b) or (c)".
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.06(1) the information must be returned and not considered | s 83.06(1)*
-- src:1492 | Return of information
-- src:1493 | 83.06 (1) For the purposes of subsection 83.05(6), any information that is obtained in confidence from a government, an institution or an agency of a foreign state, from an international organization of states or from an institution or an agency of an international organization of states and that is provided to the judge by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness shall be returned to counsel representing the Minister and shall not be considered by the judge in making the determination under paragraph 83.05(6)(d), if
-- src:1494 | (a) the judge determines that the information is not relevant;
-- src:1495 | (b) the judge determines that the information is relevant but should be summarized in a statement to be provided to the applicant; or
-- src:1496 | (c) the Minister withdraws the information.
@ref s 83.06(1) (src:1492-1496)
GIVEN `the information was obtained in confidence from a government, an institution or an agency of a foreign state, from an international organization of states or from an institution or an agency of an international organization of states` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was provided to the judge by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge determines that the information is not relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge determines that the information is relevant but should be summarized in a statement to be provided to the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister withdraws the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.06(1) the information must be returned and not considered` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the information was obtained in confidence from a government, an institution or an agency of a foreign state, from an international organization of states or from an institution or an agency of an international organization of states` AND `it was provided to the judge by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any information that is obtained in confidence from a government, an institution or an agency of a foreign state"
    ELSE IF `the judge determines that the information is not relevant` OR `the judge determines that the information is relevant but should be summarized in a statement to be provided to the applicant` OR `the Minister withdraws the information`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be considered by the judge in making the determination under paragraph 83.05(6)(d), if"

