§ `Section 83.07 -- Mistaken identity`

-- (1) A power of the entity to apply: limited by its own wording to an entity with the same or a similar name that claims not to be the listed entity.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.07(1) the entity may apply in writing to the Minister for a certificate | s 83.07(1)
-- src:1499 | Mistaken identity
-- src:1500 | 83.07 (1) An entity whose name is the same as or similar to a name, appearing on the list, of a listed entity and who claims not to be that listed entity may apply in writing to the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness for a certificate stating that it is not that listed entity.
@ref s 83.07(1) (src:1499-1500)
GIVEN `its name is the same as or similar to a name, appearing on the list, of a listed entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it claims not to be that listed entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.07(1) the entity may apply in writing to the Minister for a certificate` MEANS
    IF     `its name is the same as or similar to a name, appearing on the list, of a listed entity`
       AND `it claims not to be that listed entity`
       AND `the application is in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An entity whose name is the same as or similar to a name, appearing on the list, of a listed entity and who claims not to be that listed entity may apply in writing"

-- (2) "shall, within 30 days after receiving the application, issue a certificate if he or she is satisfied that the applicant is not that listed entity".
-- As a decision: whether the duty arises, and the last day. As a regulative rule: the Minister MUST issue the certificate WITHIN 30 days (the clock is days from the receipt).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6 | s 83.07(2) the Minister must issue the certificate; s 83.07(2) the last day for issuing the certificate; s 83.07(2) the duty to issue the certificate | s 83.07(2)
