GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the applicant is not that listed entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.07(2) the Minister must issue the certificate` MEANS
    IF `the Minister is satisfied that the applicant is not that listed entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "issue a certificate if he or she is satisfied that the applicant is not that listed entity"

@ref s 83.07(2) (src:1501-1502)
GIVEN `the day on which the Minister receives the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 83.07(2) the last day for issuing the certificate` MEANS `the day on which the Minister receives the application` PLUS 30

-- The core's `Party` has no Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness (NEEDS-CORE.md), so this module declares the one it needs.
@ref s 83.07(2) (src:1501-1502)
DECLARE `s 83.07(2) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.07(2) the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness`

@ref s 83.07(2) (src:1501-1502)
DECLARE `s 83.07(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.07(2) issues a certificate stating that the applicant is not that listed entity`

@ref s 83.07(2) (src:1501-1502)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 83.07(2) party` `s 83.07(2) act`
`s 83.07(2) the duty to issue the certificate` MEANS
    PARTY `s 83.07(2) the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness`
    MUST `s 83.07(2) issues a certificate stating that the applicant is not that listed entity`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 83.07(2) the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` BECAUSE "the certificate was not issued within 30 days after the application was received"
